A||N||8||87ECO5||Items necessary to install '88 2.5 in '84 body||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||12-03-2001||12:19 PM||||I know this has been covered before but, quite frankly, I didn't know what to search on to get the proper information.<P>If I have an '88 2.5/3-speed automatic transaxle combo complete with an ECM and the wiring harness, and I have an '84 automatic donor body, what else do I need to mate these two together?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-03-2001||01:04 PM||||Possibly a different motor mount setup?  I am not sure though, if you are getting the wiring and everything, you should be all set because that is one of the main differences between those two engines.  <P>Now that I think about it, all auto trannys were the same, so the motor mount setup you have already in the car should be the same for the engine/trans that you are going to put in.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||12-03-2001||02:27 PM||||The only other thing that may be a little bit of a pain is the difference in where the engine main harness (not the ECM harness) plugs into the main harness on the car.  On the 84's only, the plug is located in the middle of the firewall below the rear window.  On all the other Fieros ever built, the plug is next to the battery way over on the right side of the engine bay.  Will probably mean a lot of splicing.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||12-03-2001||03:07 PM||||A BUNCH of stuff<P>You will need the ENTIRE 88 wire harness for the engine and cabin and the rear harness. you will need the 88 ECM because the 84 is a distributer engine and the 88 is DIS or Distributerless. <BR>I think the front wire harness may work ok but in 87 the headlight was changed and the fan relay was changed from the 84 as well so just to be sure I'd change that it. <P>If your not willing to tear down both cars it's not worth the hastle. I was going to retrofit my 84 with the engine from my 88 but it was easier to get another 84 engine. ||||reg||4
Z||000004||theogre||12-03-2001||07:18 PM||||Not a fun project at all....<P>In addition to the wire items mentioned above... the throttle cable has to be changed. <P>If it's got cruise that will need to be sorted out. 88 ECM has built in cruise brain. 84-86 doesn't.<P>On the other hand.... doing that would eliminate all the weird ass wire problems in the 84. You'd also gain ability, electrically, for pretty easy drop in of a V6.<P>I know people have used OE harnesses to upgrade to Gen 2 headlight motors. I'm not sure if that works on the 84 or not. I'm also not sure how big a pain a 2 speed cooling fan would be.<P>The end result is that you'd effectivly have an 87 Fiero in a 84 skin. (87 had DIS in the gen 1 frame.... Plus the Gen2 headlight motors.)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||12-03-2001||08:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B>I know this has been covered before but, quite frankly, I didn't know what to search on to get the proper information.<P>If I have an '88 2.5/3-speed automatic transaxle combo complete with an ECM and the wiring harness, and I have an '84 automatic donor body, what else do I need to mate these two together?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Where'd you get the motor...happen to have access to the 88 coupe chassis still?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||12-04-2001||08:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B> Where'd you get the motor...happen to have access to the 88 coupe chassis still?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't have access to the chassis.  The availability of the motor is the result of a V6 swap.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eriamjh||12-04-2001||12:20 PM||||If I may interrupt this thread with a slight tangent... I may have access to an 88 4 cylinder 5-speed that I would like to drop into my '87 4 cylinder 5-speed (After rebuilding the '88s engine and trans).<P>Is this a problem?  Would I need the ECM and harness from the 88 in my 87?  My 87 has the DIS engine, just not the one with the balance shafts (which is what I want).<P>I'm also going 5-speed to 5-speed so unless there was a major shift cable change, I think I'd be ok.||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||12-04-2001||12:58 PM||||I'm not 100% on this but I think all you would need is the throttle cable. <P>I do know the 88 engine has a MAT (Manifold Air Temp) sensor but I'm not sure the 87 does.||||reg||5
